<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/measure> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationPositive ;
    cav:judgement "-The proposal is aligned with Directive (EU) 2019/1024 of the European Parliament and of the Council that promotes the use of open data from public sector bodies and public undertaking"@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Monitoring of research projects in the domain of marine biology and dissemination of related information"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/barrier> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationNegative ;
    cav:judgement "-Criteria to ensure that these reports are of sufficient quality should be harmonised and agreed among Member States, if the BBNJ clearing house doesn't provide suitable templates."@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeOrganisationBarrier ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Monitoring of research projects in the domain of marine biology and dissemination of related information"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationPositive ;
    cav:judgement """-Article 6 sets measures around data governance
-Article 19 requires Member states to ensure that the environmental impact assessment reports are of sufficient quality"""@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Monitoring of research projects in the domain of marine biology and dissemination of related information"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/barrier> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationNegative ;
    cav:judgement "Implementation measures will have to consider harmonisation of data managed by the national authorities and the bodies set in accordance with the interinstitutional arrangements, on top of the existing international agreement guidelines."@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeSharedBarrier ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Monitoring of research projects in the domain of marine biology and dissemination of related information"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/barrier> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationNegative ;
    cav:judgement "Implementation measures will have to consider technical interoperability of systems managed by the national authorities and the bodies set in accordance with the interinstitutional arrangements."@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeStandardsBarrier ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Monitoring of research projects in the domain of marine biology and dissemination of related information"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/description/1> a iopa:BindingRequirement,
        lomo:LegalRule ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5"@en ;
    iopa:affects <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    cav:valueDescription "Member States shall ensure that collection in situ of marine genetic resources is carried out with due regard for the rights and legitimate interests of coastal states in areas within their national jurisdiction and with due regard for the interests of other states in areas beyond national jurisdiction, in accordance with the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea. For this purpose, Member States shall cooperate, as appropriate, including using the BBNJ Clearing-House Mechanism, in order to implement the provisions of this Chapter. Member States shall cooperate, as appropriate, including using the BBNJ Clearing-House Mechanism, in order to implement the provisions of this Chapter."@en ;
    lomo:establishedIn <https://data.europa.eu/eli/dl/proc/2025/173/cod/doc/com/COM_2025_173/FINAL/eng/art_5> ;
    lomo:hasCategory dd:Data,
        dd:DigitalSolutions ;
    lomo:involvesProcess <http://example.org/process/data-collection> ;
    lomo:produces <http://example.org/analysis/description/1/action> ;
    dcterms:description "Member States shall ensure that collection in situ of marine genetic resources is carried out with due regard for the rights and legitimate interests of coastal states in areas within their national jurisdiction and with due regard for the interests of other states in areas beyond national jurisdiction, in accordance with the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea. For this purpose, Member States shall cooperate, as appropriate, including using the BBNJ Clearing-House Mechanism, in order to implement the provisions of this Chapter. Member States shall cooperate, as appropriate, including using the BBNJ Clearing-House Mechanism, in order to implement the provisions of this Chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:relation <http://example.org/ie-solution/to-be-further-explored> .

